\section{Temporal, spatial and joint structures}{

See the sections of \code{\link[=fit_model]{fit_model()}}: \emph{Temporal effects} (linear trend or cyclic
spline, and how a structured trend differs from the unstructured year
effect), \emph{Spatial effects} (nearest-neighbour Gaussian process or coordinate
spline, their assumptions and requirements), \emph{Spatio-temporal models}
(additive, or with a space-time interaction) and \emph{Joint models} (sharing a
parameter, sharing a latent process with a loading, or correlated effects).
}

\section{Reproducibility}{

Every chain gets its own seed, derived from \code{seed} and saved in \code{fit$seeds};
supply \code{chain_seeds} to reuse them. The same data, specification and seeds
give identical samples whether chains run in parallel or not. Fitted objects
also store the priors, MCMC settings, model code and monitored parameters.
}

